14526,1,"An administrator can enable the Windows policy:\nComputer Configuration > Administrative Templates > System > Filesystem > Enable Win32 long paths.\n\nIts registry equivalent is REG_DWORD LongPathsEnabled = 1 under:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\FileSystem\n\nRestart affected applications; restarting Windows may also be necessary. Applications must support long paths themselves. This is not a way to override a security denial, and Shell or the target program may still reject the path. Salamander does not change this setting."
